// Fixture: circular_reference_direct_two_instance
// Rule under test: circular reference detection -- a direct, mutual `A = B`, `B = A`
// cycle between two instances via full replace (`= Source`). Neither instance can
// ever actually resolve: A's resolution depends on B's, B's depends on A's, with no
// base case. This must be rejected before any resolution is attempted.
//
// PHASE/CHECK: spec-grounded/specified, not a guess -- confirmed implemented and
// verified: phase 4 (Register), check `circular_dependency`, DFS-based, correctly
// handles both top-level and nested full-replace cycles, zero false positives on
// valid chains. Phase 4 makes sense structurally: the register phase builds the full
// instance registry (all names, all `= Source` edges) in one pass across the whole
// file before any actual resolution begins, which is exactly what lets a DFS over the
// instance-copy graph detect a cycle up front -- independent of which instance
// happens to be declared textually first. (This also confirms, as a side effect,
// that forward-referencing an instance not yet declared later in the same file is
// legal at the registration level -- the whole graph is known before resolution
// starts, not built incrementally in file order.)
//
// Same confidence level as the corrected prediction in
// domains/domain_logical_id_collision_error.gddl: this is a documented, confirmed
// implementation detail, not a genuinely open question the way (for example) the
// original bare-scalar-field phase question was before it got resolved.

define Stats
	hp = u32

Stats A = B
	hp = 1

Stats B = A
	hp = 2

